  "lineage": "UK-originated 1980s-1990s dance-club jazz fusion style integrating hard-bop and soul-jazz influences with dance-club rhythmic-foundation, hip-hop production-elements, and electronic-instrumentation. Acid Jazz Records (founded 1987 by Eddie Piller and Gilles Peterson) consolidated the canonical sound; Galliano, Brand New Heavies, Jamiroquai, Incognito, and James Taylor Quartet anchored the recording roster. Distinguished from broader 1980s-jazz-fusion by acid jazz's dance-club orientation and UK-cultural context.",
